{
  "name": "Cognitive and Behavioral Neuroscience - BS",
  "kind": "major",
  "type": "Bachelor's Degree",
  "department": "Psychology",
  "source": "https://catalog.ucsd.edu/curric/PSYC-ug.html",
  "narrative": [
    "The BS in cognitive and behavioral neuroscience (CBN) is a major jointly administered by the Departments of Psychology and Cognitive Science.",
    "Statistics must be taken for a letter grade. All lower-division courses must be passed with a minimum grade of a C- or P.",
    "All upper-division courses numbered 100-193 must be taken for a letter grade and a minimum grade of C- is required for the course to count toward the major.",
    "Courses taken Pass/Not Pass cannot be used to satisfy the upper-division major requirement.",
    "Excluded from credit toward the major are graduate seminars (2XX).",
    "A maximum of three upper-division courses toward the CBN major may be taken outside UC San Diego. (The Cognitive Science page says: A minimum of nine upper-division courses toward the CBN major must be taken at UC San Diego.)",
    "A grade point average of at least 2.0 in the upper-division major courses is required for graduation.",
    "The Cognitive Science page (catalog.ucsd.edu/curric/COGS-ug.html) also describes this jointly administered major with slightly different lists: it accepts BILD 24, allows ECE 15 or MAE 8 by petition, has a shorter research list (no PSYC 112, 113, COGS 118A, 138, 165, 170), lists PSYC 116 and HDP 110 (not PSYC 116A-B-C, HDS 110) and omits COGS 116, 118C, 165, 170 among the CBN courses; this file follows the Psychology page."
  ],
